Title: The Interview
Credit: Written by
Author: Sample Script
Draft date: 2026-08-13

INT. WAITING ROOM - MORNING

A row of plastic chairs. MIRA, 30s, checks her phone for the fourth time.

MIRA
(to herself)
Breathe. You have done harder things than this.

The door opens. DEV, 40s, holds a clipboard he never looks at.

DEV
Mira? We're ready for you.

MIRA
That's me.

DEV
It's the third door. The one that sticks.

MIRA
Everything here sticks.

DEV (CONT'D)
You get used to it.

CUT TO:

INT. OFFICE - CONTINUOUS

A desk too large for the room. DEV sits. MIRA does not.

DEV
So. Tell me about a time you *failed*.

MIRA
How much time do you have?

DEV
Forty minutes.

MIRA
(sitting at last)
Then I'll start with the small ones.

DEV
People usually start with the flattering ones.

MIRA
People usually don't get the job.

DEV
(finally looking at the clipboard)
No. They don't.

FADE OUT.
